{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And YHWH spoke to Moses and to Aaron.</b> Since Moses said, 'I am of uncircumcised lips,' the Holy One, blessed be He, joined Aaron to him to be his mouth and interpreter." "<b>And He charged them concerning the children of Israel.</b> He charged them concerning them — to lead them gently and to bear with them (Shemot Rabbah)." "<b>And concerning Pharaoh king of Egypt.</b> He charged them concerning him — to accord him honor in their speech; this is its midrash (ibid.). Its plain sense: He charged them concerning the matter of Israel and concerning his mission to Pharaoh. And what is the substance of the charge? It is spelled out in the second section, after the genealogy — except that since Moses and Aaron were mentioned, the narrative was interrupted by <b>These are the heads of their fathers' houses</b> to teach us how Moses and Aaron were born and to whom they were traced in lineage."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:47.364603449Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}